Subject: register VM materializes the slim call frame on demand

What this does:
  A nested record frame's `JSStackFrame` (embedded at `rec->sf_embed`) carried
  eight fields that duplicate fields of the record itself: `is_strict_mode`,
  `is_constructor`, `var_buf`, `arg_buf`, `arg_count`, `var_refs`,
  `var_ref_count` and `cur_gc_obj`. The record fill stored all of them on every
  JS-to-JS call, but only the cold paths read them (closure creation, the
  debugger, error paths and backtraces), while the hot return walk reads
  `var_refs`/`var_ref_count` -- and those two are deliberately kept.

  The fill now stores only the fields the hot paths need. A new
  `regvm_sf_materialize(rt, sf)` reconstructs the dropped fields from the record
  just before a cold reader inspects them; it is idempotent and a no-op for
  non-record frames (the activation's own frame, a stack-interpreter frame, a
  native frame or a coroutine's heap frame). `regvm_rec_of_sf` recovers the
  record from the frame by testing membership in the frame arena, which holds
  only records in this build (`QJS_REGVM_INLOOP_CALL` is off). The helper is
  compiled only under `QJS_REGVM_RECORD && !QJS_REGVM_INLOOP_CALL`; elsewhere
  the fields are stored as before and the helper is an empty inline.

  `is_strict_mode`, `js_get_stack_frame_at_level`, `get_var_ref` and
  `js_new_callsite_data` are the readers that now materialize first.

  Measured (`fixed.js`, i7-8700), interleaved against 0152:
  22,577.3 M -> 22,481.0 M instructions (**-0.096 G, -0.43 %**), cycles
  10,862 M -> 10,721 M (**-1.3 %**). Full gate 8 pass / 0 fail:
  22,484,061,602 / 10,724,826,403; box2d checksum exact; diff-suite 398/0/0 mono
  and threaded; leak assertion clean; peak RSS 13228 KB; test262 errors 50 (<= 64).
